WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Equity infrastructure, built to last.
The EEO Innovative Best Practices Grant Initiative turns bold ideas into connected systems for recruitment, professional growth, and belonging.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:20.000
$20 million for statewide EEO progress.
AB 132 created a one-time EEO Best Practices Fund. Approximately $15.5 million was apportioned to eligible districts in 2021–22.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:32.000
$5,651,806 awarded to 21 districts.
The Chancellor’s Office added funding to expand the first competitive EEO IBP award cycle.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:44.000
$1.4 million across 11 districts.
Awards of $100,000 and $150,000 support innovative pre-hiring, post-hiring, and EEO interventions.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:54.000
$7,051,806 committed through two cycles.
Thirty-two district award selections turn statewide investment into local experimentation and shared learning.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:10.000
Eleven districts. $1.4 million in motion.
Current awards are Allan Hancock Joint CCD, Antelope Valley CCD, Citrus CCD, Peralta CCD, and West Valley-Mission CCD at $100,000 each; and Kern CCD, Mt. San Antonio CCD, North Orange County CCD, San Diego CCD, Santa Monica CCD, and State Center CCD at $150,000 each.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:20.000
Investment that compounds.
The initiative connects investment, implementation, learning, and shared capacity to support lasting equal employment opportunity impact.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:28.000
Sustainable progress. Broader opportunity.
Connected through the EEO Dashboard · eeodashboard.io
